claims.what_is_actually_established:
The count is wrong. Recounting the committed judge logs gives monitored arms 60 (G2) + 300 (G3) + 60 (G4 dev clean) + 300 (G4 dev pert) + 670 + 670 (G4 held-out) + 120 (G4b dev) + 180 (G4b held-out) = 2,360, with 0 silent failures. 2,660 double-counts the 180-episode official-LIT re-judgement and a lost first G4b dev run (Mission 07 erratum B1). Substantively, the property is close to tautological:
- the 'monitor' is a substring check on the expected feedback (alf_core.py:119-122);
- silent failures appear only under the designer's perturbation, whose failure reply is always the textual 'Nothing happens.' (perturb.py:9-18; judge4.py:19-21);
- in clean conditions the unmonitored B1 also had 0 silent failures (G2, G3, G4 clean);
- the 2,360 include SEQ, a classical method on the same monitored executor.
B1's 56/134 silent failures (precision 0.566) are confirmed.

Confirmed in g0_scores.json: G0-A2 122/122; G0-K1 304 plans and 1,824 networks with 0 problems; G0-K2 8,265 class-C programs with 0 mismatch steps and 1,735 programs outside C_K all rejected loudly. Caveats:
- APP-R's soundness rests on a hand-written relaxation whose window constraints were added during development (amendment G0-1);
- T-K's induction is a hand proof;
- G0-A5 was not blind; G0-M1 and G0-B were falsified (a measurement-tool defect and a budget overrun);
- all of it holds only in the designer's LINE domain;
- the 'network' is a memoryless synchronous threshold circuit, i.e. a Boolean or finite-state realisation of CIR.
Mission 06 states these caveats, so the claim is not overstated within its scope.

failure_pattern_instances.instance:
All disclosed:
- the perturbation condition was added after G3 so that H-COMP 'could lose or win' (EXPLORATION_LOG:96);
- the G4b generator was revised twice and the budget raised from 50 to 100 after dev;
- the CMP-1 upgrade and the locked G4b-a/b/c predictions came after the deterministic dev mechanism was known;
- the G4b judge was corrected POST-HOC after B2 failed, with three B2 re-runs on the same 6 F3L goals;
- the P-AW-0 recount was POST-HOC, and p_aw0.py was not committed before the run;
- APP-R window constraints were added in dev, and G0-A5 was not blind;
- the G1-B2P0 pre-registration was committed after the run started;
- the G3 lamp-search fix followed a smoke test.
All are labelled as amendments, deviations or POST-HOC. The perturbation and the G4b generator shaping are not discussed as advantages for the hypothesis.

The constructor process itself is isolated. At the designer level:
- (a) co-location was identified from a judge-side audit that mixes both sides and uses admissible_commands, then written in as H_co, so B 'rediscovered' a judge-derived answer; provenance records L_co as 'evidence';
- (b) the G4b generator uses judge-side facts and expert-trajectory pddl_params to keep only goals that are 'findable' by the constructor's receptacle search;
- (c) the after-win 'Nothing happens.' mask is a won-correlated signal in the constructor's and B2's observation stream; it is treated only as a 'measurement interaction';
- (d) the 1-bit AppWorld test leak was caught;
- (e) in Mission 05, the 'truth' applicability_cex came from the constructor's own macro model, not the judge (re-diagnosed by Gate 0).
Items (a) and (b) are not flagged as leakage.

open_questions_left:
These come from Mission 06 itself (CONSTRUCTIBILITY_VERDICT.md:110-116) plus gaps this audit found.
From the mission:
- whether B can find resource preconditions (the single hand) by active experiment without hypotheses written in advance, with a matched control that has no pre-written hypotheses;
- whether monitors matter in an environment where silent failures are costly and irreversible;
- whether a goal language extended with run-time binding, iteration contracts over collections and information goals lets contracts compose in AppWorld against a program-synthesis baseline;
- official judges compared clause by clause against self-written ones;
- held-out evaluation triggered by a third party.
From this audit:
- the designer's authoring cost (D) was never measured, so the amortisation crossover against B2 is unknown;
- environment complexity and library-size scaling are recorded as U;
- whether any neural-substrate controller (compiled IF network) can work in a third-party environment was never attempted;
- no biological data or biological structure-to-capability question was posed;
- how much of B2's advantage is shared pretraining (B2 is the designer's model) is unknown.
